WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcript of "Zoom in on DNA" by yourgenome (Genome Research Limited), CC BY.
The text is the Zoom in on DNA example's transcript; the times follow the video's captions on YouTube.

1
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:08.300
Large organisms like humans are made up of organ systems

2
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.300
such as the circulatory system and digestive system.

3
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.800
These systems include a number of organs.

4
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.800
One of them is the liver.

5
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.600
Look closer, and these organs are made up of tissues.

6
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.900
And these tissues are built of cells,

7
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.400
each specialized to perform a particular function.

8
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.400
Within each cell are structures and compartments called organelles.

9
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:59.400
These include the cell membrane, mitochondria, and nucleus.

10
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.600
The nucleus contains 23 pairs of chromosomes,

11
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.200
including a pair that determine your biological sex.

12
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.500
Each chromosome is one long length of tightly coiled DNA.

13
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:34.800
Unwind it and we see the DNA is wrapped around proteins called histones.

14
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.300
The DNA is a double helix, like a twisted ladder.

15
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.000
It is made up of four nucleotides, which contain different bases:

16
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.500
adenine, cytosine, guanine and thymine.

17
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.300
A, C, G and T.

18
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.200
A always pairs with T, and C always pairs with G.

19
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:09.800
The order, or sequence, of these bases in specific sections of the DNA, called genes,

20
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.400
carries the instructions for a cell’s structure and function.

21
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.400
One copy of the entire DNA instructions for an organism is known as the genome.

22
00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.900
The genome, organized in chromosomes within the nucleus,

23
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.900
tells each specialized cell how to function with its neighbors.

24
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.400
These make the tissues that together build organs, which work in organ systems,

25
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.400
and collectively enable an organism to grow and live.
